  "lesson_10_hint_0": "Labels and the filter as before, but move <code>?spot :liesWithin ?area</code> into <code>OPTIONAL &#123; &#125;</code>.",
  "@lesson_10_hint_0": {
    "description": "Lesson 10 «OPTIONAL»: hint 1",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_10_key": "OPTIONAL = \"show it if it exists; if not, keep the row anyway\".",
  "@lesson_10_key": {
    "description": "Lesson 10 «OPTIONAL»: the key point in one sentence",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_10_note_0": "A language FILTER (cs) goes <b>outside</b> OPTIONAL if it belongs to the required part; inside OPTIONAL it restricts only the optional part.",
  "@lesson_10_note_0": {
    "description": "Lesson 10 «OPTIONAL»: note box",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_10_note_1": "To check \"there was no value\" use <code>!BOUND(?area)</code> or <code>FILTER NOT EXISTS</code> (see its own lesson).",
  "@lesson_10_note_1": {
    "description": "Lesson 10 «OPTIONAL»: note box",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_10_note_2": "If a node has several values in OPTIONAL you get several rows. For example, with inference and a transitive <code>:liesWithin</code> \"Louka v Kokořínském dole\" also gets the CHKO.",
  "@lesson_10_note_2": {
    "description": "Lesson 10 «OPTIONAL»: note box",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_10_origin_0": "name",
  "@lesson_10_origin_0": {
    "description": "Lesson 10 «OPTIONAL»: what the term rdfs:label (RDF Schema) means, a few words"
  },
  "lesson_10_task": "List the Czech labels of the spots and, if present, the areas they directly lie in. Columns: <code>?label</code>, <code>?area</code>. <i>Pole u Kutné Hory</i> must stay in the result. <div class=\"small\"><b>An area</b> is a thing of type <code>:Area</code> or one of its subclasses: a national park, CHKO, NPR or forest (for example <code>:NP_Sumava</code>, <code>:CHKO_Kokorinsko</code>, <code>:Forest_Pelhrimov</code>). A spot is linked to it by <code>:liesWithin</code>: <code>:SpotA :liesWithin :NP_CeskeSvycarsko</code>. A spot that \"lies in no area\" simply has no <code>:liesWithin</code> triple at all.</div>",
  "@lesson_10_task": {
    "description": "Lesson 10 «OPTIONAL»: task statement",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_10_term_0": "",
  "@lesson_10_term_0": {
    "description": "Lesson 10 «OPTIONAL»: short explanation of the English term «OPTIONAL» (may stay empty)"
  },
  "lesson_10_term_1": "",
  "@lesson_10_term_1": {
    "description": "Lesson 10 «OPTIONAL»: short explanation of the English term «unbound variable» (may stay empty)"
  },
  "lesson_10_theory": "<p>If some nodes lack a value but you do not want to lose their row, wrap that part in <code>OPTIONAL &#123; &#125;</code>. Without it such rows <mark>disappear</mark>.</p>\n<pre>SELECT ?label ?parent\nWHERE &#123;\n  ?a a :Forest ; rdfs:label ?label .       # all forests and their names\n  FILTER (lang(?label) = \"cs\")\n  OPTIONAL &#123; ?a :liesWithin ?parent . &#125;     # if absent, ?parent stays empty\n&#125;</pre>\n<p>Result: 2 forests. One has a \"parent\" (the area it lies in), the other does not &mdash; but it stays in the result:</p>\n<pre>Les v Jizerských horách        :CHKO_JizerskeHory\nLes u Pelhřimova               (empty)</pre>\n<p>Without OPTIONAL (<code>?a :liesWithin ?parent</code> directly in WHERE) only the first forest would remain &mdash; \"Les u Pelhřimova\" would disappear.</p>",
  "@lesson_10_theory": {
    "description": "Lesson 10 «OPTIONAL»: theory",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_10_title": "OPTIONAL",
  "@lesson_10_title": {
    "description": "Lesson 10 «OPTIONAL»: title"
  },
  "lesson_11_hint_0": "<code>ORDER BY ?label LIMIT 3</code> &mdash; after <code>&#125;</code>.",
  "@lesson_11_hint_0": {
    "description": "Lesson 11 «ORDER BY and LIMIT»: hint 1",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_11_key": "ORDER BY = order, LIMIT = how many rows; both go after &#125;.",
  "@lesson_11_key": {
    "description": "Lesson 11 «ORDER BY and LIMIT»: the key point in one sentence",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_11_note_0": "<code>ORDER BY</code> and <code>LIMIT</code> come <b>after</b> <code>&#125;</code>, not inside WHERE.",
  "@lesson_11_note_0": {
    "description": "Lesson 11 «ORDER BY and LIMIT»: note box",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_11_note_1": "Without <code>ORDER BY</code> the row order is not guaranteed and may differ between runs and tools. If the task requires an order, write <code>ORDER BY</code>.",
  "@lesson_11_note_1": {
    "description": "Lesson 11 «ORDER BY and LIMIT»: note box",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_11_note_2": "<code>LIMIT 3</code> without <code>ORDER BY</code> returns \"some\" 3 rows, not necessarily the first alphabetically.",
  "@lesson_11_note_2": {
    "description": "Lesson 11 «ORDER BY and LIMIT»: note box",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_11_note_3": "<code>ASC(?x)</code> = ascending, <code>DESC(?x)</code> = descending. If no direction is given it is <code>ASC</code>: <code>ORDER BY ?x</code> = <code>ORDER BY ASC(?x)</code>.",
  "@lesson_11_note_3": {
    "description": "Lesson 11 «ORDER BY and LIMIT»: note box",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_11_origin_0": "name",
  "@lesson_11_origin_0": {
