  "lesson_11_theory": "<p>Sorting and limiting rows are written <mark>after</mark> the closing brace of WHERE:</p>\n<pre>SELECT ?name\nWHERE &#123; ?park a :NationalPark ; rdfs:label ?name . FILTER (lang(?name) = \"cs\") &#125;\nORDER BY DESC(?name)       # Z to A\nLIMIT 2                    # only the first 2</pre>\n<p>Result: \"Národní park Šumava\", \"Národní park České Švýcarsko\" (descending order).</p>\n<p>Two sort directions:</p>\n<pre>ORDER BY ASC(?name)      # ascending:  A &rarr; Z, 1 &rarr; 9 (old &rarr; new for dates)\nORDER BY DESC(?name)     # descending: Z &rarr; A, 9 &rarr; 1\nORDER BY ?name           # same as ASC(?name): ascending is the default</pre>\n<p>Sorting by several columns (each can have its own direction):</p>\n<pre>ORDER BY ?type DESC(?n)            # first by type (A&rarr;Z), ties by count (high &rarr; low)\nORDER BY DESC(?n) ASC(?name)       # first by count (high &rarr; low), ties by name (A &rarr; Z)\nORDER BY DESC(?n) ?name            # the same: ASC may be omitted</pre>",
  "@lesson_11_theory": {
    "description": "Lesson 11 «ORDER BY and LIMIT»: theory",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_11_title": "ORDER BY and LIMIT",
  "@lesson_11_title": {
    "description": "Lesson 11 «ORDER BY and LIMIT»: title"
  },
  "lesson_12_hint_0": "You need the patterns <code>?stay :atSpot ?spot</code> and <code>?spot rdfs:label ?spotLabel</code> (+ the cs filter).",
  "@lesson_12_hint_0": {
    "description": "Lesson 12 «GROUP BY and COUNT»: hint 1",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_12_hint_1": "Group by <code>?spotLabel</code>.",
  "@lesson_12_hint_1": {
    "description": "Lesson 12 «GROUP BY and COUNT»: hint 2",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_12_hint_2": "<code>ORDER BY DESC(?stays) ?spotLabel</code>",
  "@lesson_12_hint_2": {
    "description": "Lesson 12 «GROUP BY and COUNT»: hint 3",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_12_key": "COUNT counts rows in a group. SELECT may contain only the grouped variables and aggregates.",
  "@lesson_12_key": {
    "description": "Lesson 12 «GROUP BY and COUNT»: the key point in one sentence",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_12_note_0": "In <code>SELECT</code> you may keep <b>only</b> the variables from <code>GROUP BY</code> and aggregates. Any other variable is an error.",
  "@lesson_12_note_0": {
    "description": "Lesson 12 «GROUP BY and COUNT»: note box",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_12_note_1": "An aggregate needs its parentheses and <code>AS</code>: <code>(COUNT(?stay) AS ?stays)</code>. Without them it is a syntax error.",
  "@lesson_12_note_1": {
    "description": "Lesson 12 «GROUP BY and COUNT»: note box",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_12_note_2": "Spots without stays <b>do not appear</b> in the result (nothing to count). To show 0 you need <code>OPTIONAL</code> + <code>COUNT(?x)</code> (see task 4).",
  "@lesson_12_note_2": {
    "description": "Lesson 12 «GROUP BY and COUNT»: note box",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_12_note_3": "<code>COUNT(DISTINCT ?x)</code> counts distinct values. With inference and paths you often need exactly this: otherwise one entity is counted several times.",
  "@lesson_12_note_3": {
    "description": "Lesson 12 «GROUP BY and COUNT»: note box",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_12_origin_0": "subclass",
  "@lesson_12_origin_0": {
    "description": "Lesson 12 «GROUP BY and COUNT»: what the term rdfs:subClassOf (RDF Schema) means, a few words"
  },
  "lesson_12_task": "How many stays are at each spot? Columns: <code>?spotLabel</code> (Czech label), <code>?stays</code>. Order by count descending, then by label.",
