  "lesson_12_theory": "<p>To <mark>count</mark> how many of something, group rows (<code>GROUP BY</code>) and apply an aggregate: <code>COUNT, SUM, AVG, MIN, MAX, GROUP_CONCAT</code>.</p>\n<pre>SELECT ?type (COUNT(?area) AS ?n)             # count areas, name the result ?n\nWHERE &#123;\n  ?area a ?type .                             # the area has a type\n  ?type rdfs:subClassOf :ProtectedArea .      # and that type is a kind of protected area\n&#125;\nGROUP BY ?type                               # separately for each type\nORDER BY DESC(?n)</pre>\n<p>Result &mdash; how many areas of each type:</p>\n<pre>:NationalPark              4\n:ProtectedLandscapeArea    3\n:NationalNatureReserve     1</pre>\n<p>Other aggregates:</p>\n<pre>(COUNT(DISTINCT ?x) AS ?n)                          # without duplicates\n(GROUP_CONCAT(?l; separator=\", \") AS ?all)          # join values into one cell\n(MIN(?x) AS ?first)  (MAX(?x) AS ?last)             # smallest / largest</pre>",
  "@lesson_12_theory": {
    "description": "Lesson 12 «GROUP BY and COUNT»: theory",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_12_title": "GROUP BY and COUNT",
  "@lesson_12_title": {
    "description": "Lesson 12 «GROUP BY and COUNT»: title"
  },
  "lesson_13_hint_0": "A subclass is written as <code>?class rdfs:subClassOf :Activity</code>.",
  "@lesson_13_hint_0": {
    "description": "Lesson 13 «Property paths: / and *»: hint 1",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_13_hint_1": "The star also includes <code>:Activity</code> itself (0 steps): <code>rdfs:subClassOf*</code>.",
  "@lesson_13_hint_1": {
    "description": "Lesson 13 «Property paths: / and *»: hint 2",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_13_key": "The star * includes the starting node itself (0 steps); the plus + does not.",
  "@lesson_13_key": {
    "description": "Lesson 13 «Property paths: / and *»: the key point in one sentence",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_13_note_0": "Paths work <b>without inference</b>: the engine follows the chain while executing the query.",
  "@lesson_13_note_0": {
    "description": "Lesson 13 «Property paths: / and *»: note box",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_13_note_1": "<code>*</code> also returns the start node itself (<code>:Activity</code>). If you do not want it use <code>+</code>.",
  "@lesson_13_note_1": {
    "description": "Lesson 13 «Property paths: / and *»: note box",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_13_note_2": "<code>a/rdfs:subClassOf*</code> is usually written <b>without spaces</b> around <code>/</code>; spaces are allowed, but do not forget the <code>/</code>.",
  "@lesson_13_note_2": {
    "description": "Lesson 13 «Property paths: / and *»: note box",
    "context": "html"
  },
