  "lesson_13_theory": "<p>A path lets you follow several relations at once without intermediate variables.</p>\n<table><tr><td><code>p1/p2</code></td><td>first p1, then p2</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>p*</code></td><td>zero or more steps of p</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>p+</code></td><td>one or more steps</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>^p</code></td><td>against the direction</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>p1|p2</code></td><td>either p1 or p2</td></tr></table>\n<p><b>Sequence /</b> &mdash; spot &rarr; the area it lies in &rarr; that area's English name:</p>\n<pre>SELECT ?spot ?areaName\nWHERE &#123; ?spot :liesWithin/rdfs:label ?areaName .\n        FILTER (lang(?areaName) = \"en\") &#125;\n# same as: ?spot :liesWithin ?x . ?x rdfs:label ?areaName .</pre>\n<p>Result: SpotA &rarr; \"Bohemian Switzerland National Park\", SpotC &rarr; \"Forest in the Jizera Mountains\", SpotE &rarr; \"Forest near Pelhřimov\".</p>\n<p><b>Star *</b> &mdash; a class and all its subclasses (<code>rdfs:subClassOf</code> = \"subclass\", <b>RDFS</b> vocabulary):</p>\n<pre>SELECT ?class\nWHERE &#123; ?class rdfs:subClassOf* :Area . &#125;</pre>\n<p>Result (6 rows): <code>:Area</code> (0 steps), <code>:ProtectedArea</code>, <code>:Forest</code>, <code>:NationalPark</code>, <code>:ProtectedLandscapeArea</code>, <code>:NationalNatureReserve</code>. Without the star only the direct subclasses <code>:ProtectedArea</code> and <code>:Forest</code>.</p>",
  "@lesson_13_theory": {
    "description": "Lesson 13 «Property paths: / and *»: theory",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_13_title": "Property paths: / and *",
  "@lesson_13_title": {
    "description": "Lesson 13 «Property paths: / and *»: title"
  },
  "lesson_14_hint_0": "<code>?spot a :Spot ; :liesWithin+ ?area .</code>",
