  },
  "lesson_14_note_0": "<code>:liesWithin</code> is our property from bivak.ttl; the data declares it transitive (<code>owl:TransitiveProperty</code>, <b>OWL</b> vocabulary), but the <code>+</code> path works regardless.",
  "@lesson_14_note_0": {
    "description": "Lesson 14 «Transitive path +»: note box",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_14_note_1": "If a spot lies nowhere (SpotD) the <code>+</code> path gives no row for it. To keep it (with 0) you need <code>OPTIONAL</code>.",
  "@lesson_14_note_1": {
    "description": "Lesson 14 «Transitive path +»: note box",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_14_note_2": "<code>+</code> = \"at least one step\", <code>*</code> = \"zero or more\". For \"all areas above\" use <code>+</code>.",
  "@lesson_14_note_2": {
    "description": "Lesson 14 «Transitive path +»: note box",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_14_origin_0": "transitive property",
