    "description": "Lesson 14 «Transitive path +»: short explanation of the English term «lies within» (may stay empty)"
  },
  "lesson_14_theory": "<p>An area may lie in another area, which lies in a third. The direct <code>:liesWithin</code> gives only <b>one step</b>. The path <code>:liesWithin+</code> follows the <mark>whole chain</mark> to the end.</p>\n<pre>SELECT ?up\nWHERE &#123; :NPR_KokorinskyDul :liesWithin+ ?up . &#125;     # what contains NPR Kokořínský důl\n# result: :CHKO_Kokorinsko</pre>\n<p>The path can also be followed \"backwards\" &mdash; ask <b>what lies inside</b>:</p>\n<pre>SELECT ?x\nWHERE &#123; ?x :liesWithin+ :CHKO_Kokorinsko . &#125;        # everything inside CHKO Kokořínsko</pre>\n<p>Result: <code>:NPR_KokorinskyDul</code> (directly), <code>:SpotF</code> (directly), <code>:SpotB</code> (through the NPR). Without <code>+</code> (plain <code>:liesWithin</code>) <code>:SpotB</code> would not be found: it lies in the NPR, not in the CHKO.</p>\n<p>Chains in the data:</p>\n<pre>:SpotB &rarr; :NPR_KokorinskyDul &rarr; :CHKO_Kokorinsko\n:SpotC &rarr; :Forest_JizerskeHory &rarr; :CHKO_JizerskeHory</pre>",
  "@lesson_14_theory": {
    "description": "Lesson 14 «Transitive path +»: theory",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_14_title": "Transitive path +",
  "@lesson_14_title": {
    "description": "Lesson 14 «Transitive path +»: title"
  },
  "lesson_15_hint_0": "<code>?spot :liesWithin+ ?area . ?area a/rdfs:subClassOf* :ProtectedArea .</code>",
  "@lesson_15_hint_0": {
    "description": "Lesson 15 «Type via a/subClassOf*»: hint 1",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_15_hint_1": "The spot's label + the cs filter, and <code>SELECT DISTINCT</code>.",
  "@lesson_15_hint_1": {
    "description": "Lesson 15 «Type via a/subClassOf*»: hint 2",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_15_key": "a/rdfs:subClassOf* = \"has this type, counting subclasses\".",
  "@lesson_15_key": {
    "description": "Lesson 15 «Type via a/subClassOf*»: the key point in one sentence",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_15_note_0": "<code>a</code> is <code>rdf:type</code> (<b>RDF</b>); <code>rdfs:subClassOf</code> is <b>RDFS</b>. Both walk the class hierarchy, <code>/</code> glues them.",
  "@lesson_15_note_0": {
    "description": "Lesson 15 «Type via a/subClassOf*»: note box",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_15_note_1": "<code>:Spot</code> is not a subclass of <code>:Area</code> in bivak.ttl. The path <code>?s a/rdfs:subClassOf* :Area</code> will not find a spot.",
  "@lesson_15_note_1": {
    "description": "Lesson 15 «Type via a/subClassOf*»: note box",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_15_note_2": "The same trick underlies the queries about restrictions (UNION lesson) and category \"overlap\".",
  "@lesson_15_note_2": {
    "description": "Lesson 15 «Type via a/subClassOf*»: note box",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_15_origin_0": "type of a thing (shortcut a)",
  "@lesson_15_origin_0": {
    "description": "Lesson 15 «Type via a/subClassOf*»: what the term rdf:type (RDF) means, a few words"
  },
  "lesson_15_origin_1": "subclass",
  "@lesson_15_origin_1": {
    "description": "Lesson 15 «Type via a/subClassOf*»: what the term rdfs:subClassOf (RDF Schema) means, a few words"
  },
  "lesson_15_task": "Find the spots that lie (directly or indirectly) in any protected area (<code>:ProtectedArea</code>, including its subclasses). Return the distinct Czech labels. Column: <code>?label</code>. <div class=\"small\"><b>An area</b> is a thing of type <code>:Area</code> or one of its subclasses: a national park, CHKO, NPR or forest (for example <code>:NP_Sumava</code>, <code>:CHKO_Kokorinsko</code>, <code>:Forest_Pelhrimov</code>). A spot is linked to it by <code>:liesWithin</code>: <code>:SpotA :liesWithin :NP_CeskeSvycarsko</code>. A spot that \"lies in no area\" simply has no <code>:liesWithin</code> triple at all.</div>",
  "@lesson_15_task": {
    "description": "Lesson 15 «Type via a/subClassOf*»: task statement",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_15_term_0": "",
  "@lesson_15_term_0": {
    "description": "Lesson 15 «Type via a/subClassOf*»: short explanation of the English term «class hierarchy» (may stay empty)"
  },
  "lesson_15_term_1": "",
  "@lesson_15_term_1": {
    "description": "Lesson 15 «Type via a/subClassOf*»: short explanation of the English term «subclass of» (may stay empty)"
  },
  "lesson_15_term_2": "",
  "@lesson_15_term_2": {
    "description": "Lesson 15 «Type via a/subClassOf*»: short explanation of the English term «instance of» (may stay empty)"
  },
  "lesson_15_theory": "<p>You often need to check that a node belongs to a class <b>\"or any of its subclasses\"</b>. Join two relations into one path:</p>\n<pre>?x a/rdfs:subClassOf* :Shelter\n#   └ type of node  └ up the class hierarchy</pre>\n<p>Hierarchy in the data: <code>:NationalPark</code> &sube; <code>:ProtectedArea</code> &sube; <code>:Area</code>; <code>:Forest</code> &sube; <code>:Area</code>. For shelters: <code>:Tent</code>, <code>:Tarp</code>, <code>:Hammock</code>, <code>:BivySack</code> &sube; <code>:Shelter</code>.</p>\n<pre># all shelters of stays, any kind (6 blank nodes)\nSELECT ?shelter WHERE &#123; ?stay :usesShelter ?shelter . ?shelter a/rdfs:subClassOf* :Shelter . &#125;\n\n# only \"forest\" areas (direct type, no hierarchy)\nSELECT ?area WHERE &#123; ?area a :Forest . &#125;</pre>\n<p>Without inference the query <code>?x a :Shelter</code> returns 0: nobody has that type directly. The path solves this without inference.</p>\n<p>Idea: when the task says \"<i>including subclasses</i>\", add <code>/rdfs:subClassOf*</code> after <code>a</code>.</p>",
  "@lesson_15_theory": {
    "description": "Lesson 15 «Type via a/subClassOf*»: theory",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_15_title": "Type via a/subClassOf*",
  "@lesson_15_title": {
    "description": "Lesson 15 «Type via a/subClassOf*»: title"
  },
  "lesson_16_hint_0": "Do not know a restriction's structure? Explore it: <code>SELECT ?p ?o WHERE &#123; :OvernightBan_CS ?p ?o &#125;</code> (lesson 6).",
  "@lesson_16_hint_0": {
    "description": "Lesson 16 «UNION and VALUES (harder)»: hint 1",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_16_hint_1": "Start: <code>:SpotA :liesWithin+ ?area .</code>",
  "@lesson_16_hint_1": {
    "description": "Lesson 16 «UNION and VALUES (harder)»: hint 2",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_16_hint_2": "Two UNION branches: in one <code>?r :appliesToArea ?area</code>, in the other the area's type (<code>?area a/rdfs:subClassOf* ?type</code>) and <code>?r :appliesToAreaType ?type</code>; after them <code>?r rdfs:label ?restrictionLabel</code>.",
  "@lesson_16_hint_2": {
    "description": "Lesson 16 «UNION and VALUES (harder)»: hint 3",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_16_hint_3": "Do not forget <code>FILTER (lang(?restrictionLabel) = \"cs\")</code> and <code>DISTINCT</code>.",
  "@lesson_16_hint_3": {
    "description": "Lesson 16 «UNION and VALUES (harder)»: hint 4",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_16_key": "UNION = \"or\": it merges the results of two patterns.",
  "@lesson_16_key": {
    "description": "Lesson 16 «UNION and VALUES (harder)»: the key point in one sentence",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_16_note_0": "Each UNION branch goes in its own braces <code>&#123; … &#125;</code>; without braces the query cannot be parsed.",
  "@lesson_16_note_0": {
    "description": "Lesson 16 «UNION and VALUES (harder)»: note box",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_16_note_1": "UNION returns rows of <b>both</b> branches, so you often need <code>SELECT DISTINCT</code>: one restriction may be found in both.",
  "@lesson_16_note_1": {
    "description": "Lesson 16 «UNION and VALUES (harder)»: note box",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_16_note_2": "<code>VALUES</code> is a list of \"substitutions\": the query runs once per value. Handy to avoid writing a query twice.",
  "@lesson_16_note_2": {
    "description": "Lesson 16 «UNION and VALUES (harder)»: note box",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_16_origin_0": "name",
  "@lesson_16_origin_0": {
    "description": "Lesson 16 «UNION and VALUES (harder)»: what the term rdfs:label (RDF Schema) means, a few words"
  },
  "lesson_16_task": "Which restrictions apply to the spot <code>:SpotA</code>? A <b>restriction</b> is a thing of type <code>:Restriction</code> (for example <code>:OvernightBan_CS</code>) with a name <code>rdfs:label</code> (in cs and en). It is attached to an area in one of two ways: <code>?r :appliesToArea ?area</code> (a specific area) or <code>?r :appliesToAreaType ?type</code> (a whole type of areas; the area's class or one of its superclasses). The spot's areas: <code>:SpotA :liesWithin+ ?area</code>. Return the distinct Czech restriction labels. Column: <code>?restrictionLabel</code>. <div class=\"small\"><b>An area</b> is a thing of type <code>:Area</code> or one of its subclasses: a national park, CHKO, NPR or forest (for example <code>:NP_Sumava</code>, <code>:CHKO_Kokorinsko</code>, <code>:Forest_Pelhrimov</code>). A spot is linked to it by <code>:liesWithin</code>: <code>:SpotA :liesWithin :NP_CeskeSvycarsko</code>. A spot that \"lies in no area\" simply has no <code>:liesWithin</code> triple at all.</div>",
  "@lesson_16_task": {
    "description": "Lesson 16 «UNION and VALUES (harder)»: task statement",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_16_term_0": "",
  "@lesson_16_term_0": {
    "description": "Lesson 16 «UNION and VALUES (harder)»: short explanation of the English term «UNION» (may stay empty)"
  },
  "lesson_16_term_1": "",
  "@lesson_16_term_1": {
    "description": "Lesson 16 «UNION and VALUES (harder)»: short explanation of the English term «VALUES» (may stay empty)"
  },
  "lesson_16_term_2": "",
  "@lesson_16_term_2": {
    "description": "Lesson 16 «UNION and VALUES (harder)»: short explanation of the English term «restriction» (may stay empty)"
  },
  "lesson_16_term_3": "",
  "@lesson_16_term_3": {
    "description": "Lesson 16 «UNION and VALUES (harder)»: short explanation of the English term «applies to» (may stay empty)"
  },
  "lesson_16_theory": "<p><code>&#123; A &#125; UNION &#123; B &#125;</code> &mdash; rows found <mark>either by A or by B</mark> match. Use it when the same question can be asked in two ways.</p>\n<pre># national parks OR CHKO (7 areas)\nSELECT ?a WHERE &#123;\n  &#123; ?a a :NationalPark &#125;\n  UNION\n  &#123; ?a a :ProtectedLandscapeArea &#125;\n&#125;</pre>\n<p><code>VALUES</code> sets ?x by hand to a list of values &mdash; the query runs once for each:</p>\n<pre>SELECT ?a WHERE &#123;\n  VALUES ?t &#123; :NationalNatureReserve :Forest &#125;     # ?t takes the two values in turn\n  ?a a ?t .\n&#125;                                                   # NPR Kokořínský důl + two forests</pre>\n<p><b>Data for the task.</b> A restriction (<code>:Restriction</code>) can be attached to an area in <i>two different ways</i>:</p>\n<pre>:OvernightBan_CS    :appliesToArea     :NP_CeskeSvycarsko .   # to a specific area\n:CampingBan_Forest  :appliesToAreaType :Forest .           # to a whole type of areas</pre>\n<p>Think: how do you check that a restriction applies to <b>the spot's area</b> in both variants? Each variant is its own UNION branch. Get the spot's areas with <code>:liesWithin+</code>.</p>",
  "@lesson_16_theory": {
    "description": "Lesson 16 «UNION and VALUES (harder)»: theory",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_16_title": "UNION and VALUES (harder)",
  "@lesson_16_title": {
    "description": "Lesson 16 «UNION and VALUES (harder)»: title"
  },
  "lesson_17_hint_0": "Paths: <code>?stay :usesShelter/a/rdfs:subClassOf* :Tent</code> and <code>?stay :includesActivity/a/rdfs:subClassOf* :CampActivity</code>.",
  "@lesson_17_hint_0": {
    "description": "Lesson 17 «BIND, IF, EXISTS»: hint 1",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_17_hint_1": "Join the two <code>EXISTS</code> with <code>||</code> inside <code>IF(…)</code>.",
  "@lesson_17_hint_1": {
    "description": "Lesson 17 «BIND, IF, EXISTS»: hint 2",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_17_key": "BIND + IF + EXISTS = compute a new column from a condition.",
  "@lesson_17_key": {
    "description": "Lesson 17 «BIND, IF, EXISTS»: the key point in one sentence",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_17_note_0": "A variable from <code>BIND (… AS ?x)</code> cannot be used in WHERE <b>before</b> the BIND itself: place BIND after the patterns where its input variables are defined.",
  "@lesson_17_note_0": {
    "description": "Lesson 17 «BIND, IF, EXISTS»: note box",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_17_note_1": "Combine two checks with <code>||</code> (\"or\") or <code>&amp;&amp;</code> (\"and\") <b>inside</b> IF: <code>IF(EXISTS&#123;…&#125; || EXISTS&#123;…&#125;, a, b)</code>.",
  "@lesson_17_note_1": {
    "description": "Lesson 17 «BIND, IF, EXISTS»: note box",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_17_note_2": "The paths <code>:usesShelter/a/rdfs:subClassOf* :Tent</code> take subclasses into account: if a <code>:BigTent &sube; :Tent</code> appears it is covered too.",
  "@lesson_17_note_2": {
    "description": "Lesson 17 «BIND, IF, EXISTS»: note box",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_17_task": "Classify each stay: <code>:Camping</code> if it uses a tent (<code>:Tent</code> or subclass) or includes a <code>:CampActivity</code> (or subclass), otherwise <code>:Bivouacking</code>. Columns: <code>?stayLabel</code> (Czech), <code>?kind</code>.",
  "@lesson_17_task": {
    "description": "Lesson 17 «BIND, IF, EXISTS»: task statement",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_17_term_0": "",
  "@lesson_17_term_0": {
    "description": "Lesson 17 «BIND, IF, EXISTS»: short explanation of the English term «BIND» (may stay empty)"
  },
  "lesson_17_term_1": "",
  "@lesson_17_term_1": {
    "description": "Lesson 17 «BIND, IF, EXISTS»: short explanation of the English term «IF(cond, a, b)» (may stay empty)"
  },
  "lesson_17_term_2": "",
  "@lesson_17_term_2": {
    "description": "Lesson 17 «BIND, IF, EXISTS»: short explanation of the English term «EXISTS» (may stay empty)"
  },
  "lesson_17_term_3": "",
  "@lesson_17_term_3": {
    "description": "Lesson 17 «BIND, IF, EXISTS»: short explanation of the English term «computed column» (may stay empty)"
  },
  "lesson_17_theory": "<p><code>BIND (… AS ?x)</code> creates a new column. <code>IF(condition, yes, no)</code> picks a value. <code>EXISTS &#123; … &#125;</code> checks whether anything matches a pattern.</p>\n<pre># for each area: nested or top-level\nSELECT ?a ?level WHERE &#123;\n  ?a a/rdfs:subClassOf* :Area .\n  BIND ( IF (EXISTS &#123; ?a :liesWithin ?parent &#125;,\n             \"nested\",          # yes\n             \"top-level\")       # no\n         AS ?level )\n&#125;</pre>\n<p>Result: 10 rows; \"nested\" only for <code>:NPR_KokorinskyDul</code> and <code>:Forest_JizerskeHory</code>, the other 8 are \"top-level\".</p>\n<p>Conditions combine: <code>IF(EXISTS&#123;…&#125; || EXISTS&#123;…&#125;, a, b)</code> is \"or\", <code>&amp;&amp;</code> is \"and\". A plain BIND without IF &mdash; for example concatenating text:</p>\n<pre>BIND (CONCAT(\"Area: \", ?label) AS ?title)</pre>",
  "@lesson_17_theory": {
    "description": "Lesson 17 «BIND, IF, EXISTS»: theory",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_17_title": "BIND, IF, EXISTS",
  "@lesson_17_title": {
    "description": "Lesson 17 «BIND, IF, EXISTS»: title"
  },
  "lesson_18_hint_0": "<code>?area a/rdfs:subClassOf* :Area ; rdfs:label ?label .</code>",
  "@lesson_18_hint_0": {
    "description": "Lesson 18 «FILTER NOT EXISTS»: hint 1",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_18_hint_1": "<code>FILTER NOT EXISTS &#123; ?area rdfs:label ?en . FILTER (lang(?en) = \"en\") &#125;</code>",
  "@lesson_18_hint_1": {
    "description": "Lesson 18 «FILTER NOT EXISTS»: hint 2",
