  },
  "lesson_18_hint_2": "You need <code>DISTINCT</code>.",
  "@lesson_18_hint_2": {
    "description": "Lesson 18 «FILTER NOT EXISTS»: hint 3",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_18_key": "NOT EXISTS = \"nothing like that can be found\".",
  "@lesson_18_key": {
    "description": "Lesson 18 «FILTER NOT EXISTS»: the key point in one sentence",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_18_note_0": "Inside <code>NOT EXISTS</code> use the <b>same variable</b> as outside (<code>?area</code>), otherwise the condition links nothing.",
  "@lesson_18_note_0": {
    "description": "Lesson 18 «FILTER NOT EXISTS»: note box",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_18_note_1": "Alternative: <code>OPTIONAL &#123; … &#125;</code> + <code>FILTER (!BOUND(?x))</code>. <code>NOT EXISTS</code> is shorter and clearer.",
  "@lesson_18_note_1": {
    "description": "Lesson 18 «FILTER NOT EXISTS»: note box",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_18_note_2": "You need <code>DISTINCT</code> if an area has several labels: it would otherwise appear once per label.",
  "@lesson_18_note_2": {
    "description": "Lesson 18 «FILTER NOT EXISTS»: note box",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_18_origin_0": "name",
  "@lesson_18_origin_0": {
    "description": "Lesson 18 «FILTER NOT EXISTS»: what the term rdfs:label (RDF Schema) means, a few words"
  },
  "lesson_18_task": "Which areas (type <code>:Area</code> or its subclass) have no English label? Return the distinct <code>?area</code> and <code>?label</code> (any label). <div class=\"small\"><b>An area</b> is a thing of type <code>:Area</code> or one of its subclasses: a national park, CHKO, NPR or forest (for example <code>:NP_Sumava</code>, <code>:CHKO_Kokorinsko</code>, <code>:Forest_Pelhrimov</code>). A spot is linked to it by <code>:liesWithin</code>: <code>:SpotA :liesWithin :NP_CeskeSvycarsko</code>. A spot that \"lies in no area\" simply has no <code>:liesWithin</code> triple at all.</div>",
  "@lesson_18_task": {
    "description": "Lesson 18 «FILTER NOT EXISTS»: task statement",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_18_term_0": "",
  "@lesson_18_term_0": {
    "description": "Lesson 18 «FILTER NOT EXISTS»: short explanation of the English term «NOT EXISTS» (may stay empty)"
  },
  "lesson_18_term_1": "",
  "@lesson_18_term_1": {
    "description": "Lesson 18 «FILTER NOT EXISTS»: short explanation of the English term «missing value» (may stay empty)"
  },
  "lesson_18_theory": "<p><code>FILTER NOT EXISTS &#123; … &#125;</code> keeps only rows for which the inner pattern <mark>finds nothing</mark>. This is how you look for \"something is missing\".</p>\n<pre># stays where NO food is prepared\nSELECT ?label WHERE &#123;\n  ?stay :atSpot ?spot ; rdfs:label ?label .\n  FILTER (lang(?label) = \"cs\")\n  FILTER NOT EXISTS &#123; ?stay :includesActivity/a :FoodPreparation &#125;\n&#125;</pre>\n<p>Result: 4 of 6 stays &mdash; \"Celta pod převisem\", \"Hamaka v Jizerkách\", \"Jen spacák v Kokořínském dole\", \"Stan v lese u Pelhřimova\". The two stays with food (\"Stan na poli\", \"Celta a vaření…\") are removed.</p>\n<p>Scheme: the outer part selects candidates, <code>NOT EXISTS</code> adds \"and there must be no such thing\". Inside, use the <b>same variable</b> as outside (<code>?stay</code>), otherwise nothing is linked.</p>\n<p>Inside <code>NOT EXISTS</code> any pattern may stand: a path, a language filter, etc.</p>",
  "@lesson_18_theory": {
    "description": "Lesson 18 «FILTER NOT EXISTS»: theory",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_18_title": "FILTER NOT EXISTS",
  "@lesson_18_title": {
    "description": "Lesson 18 «FILTER NOT EXISTS»: title"
  },
