  "lesson_19_theory": "<p><code>ASK &#123; … &#125;</code> returns no table &mdash; only <mark>yes/no</mark> (<code>true</code>/<code>false</code>): was at least one match found.</p>\n<pre>ASK &#123; :Stay1 :usesShelter/a :Tent . &#125;          # false: Stay1 has a tarp, not a tent\nASK &#123; :Stay5 :usesShelter/a :Tent . &#125;          # true</pre>\n<p>More complex questions the same way:</p>\n<pre># Is there a national park that lies in something else?\nASK &#123; ?p a :NationalPark ; :liesWithin ?x . &#125;  # false\n\n# Is there a stay without food preparation?\nASK &#123; ?s :atSpot ?x .\n      FILTER NOT EXISTS &#123; ?s :includesActivity/a :FoodPreparation &#125; &#125;   # true</pre>\n<p>The pattern inside ASK is the same as in the WHERE of a SELECT: with all the paths, FILTER, NOT EXISTS.</p>",
  "@lesson_19_theory": {
    "description": "Lesson 19 «ASK»: theory",
    "context": "html"
  },
