  "lesson_23_theory": "<p>SKOS is a vocabulary of concepts (a W3C standard, prefix <code>skos:</code>). Instead of the string <code>\"CHKO\"</code> the data holds a <mark>concept</mark> with labels in several languages, a code, a definition and a parent. All terms below are from the <b>SKOS</b> vocabulary:</p>\n<pre>kat:CHKO a skos:Concept ;                           # a concept\n    skos:inScheme kat:schema ;                      # which vocabulary\n    skos:broader kat:VZCHU ;                        # parent (broader)\n    skos:prefLabel \"Chráněná krajinná oblast\"@cs ,  # main name (one per language)\n                   \"Protected landscape area\"@en ;\n    skos:altLabel \"CHKO\"@cs ;                       # synonym, abbreviation\n    skos:notation \"CHKO\" ;                          # code from the data table\n    skos:definition \"Rozsáhlé území …\"@cs ;         # what it means\n    skos:closeMatch iucn:V .                        # nearly the same in another vocabulary</pre>\n<p>And the vocabulary (scheme) itself with a top concept:</p>\n<pre>kat:schema a skos:ConceptScheme ;\n    skos:hasTopConcept kat:VZCHU .</pre>\n<p><code>kat:</code>, <code>iucn:</code> are <b>our</b> course prefixes (protection categories, IUCN categories); <code>skos:</code> is the standard.</p>\n<p><code>skos:exactMatch</code> = \"the same concept in another vocabulary\" (only for interchangeable ones), <code>skos:closeMatch</code> = \"nearly the same\".</p>",
  "@lesson_23_theory": {
    "description": "Lesson 23 «SKOS: one concept»: theory",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_23_title": "SKOS: one concept",
  "@lesson_23_title": {
    "description": "Lesson 23 «SKOS: one concept»: title"
  },
