  "lesson_24_theory": "<p>The concept hierarchy (who is \"broader\") is walked with a path just like classes. But <code>skos:broader</code> (<b>SKOS</b> vocabulary) is <b>not</b> <code>rdfs:subClassOf</code>: it links concepts of a vocabulary.</p>\n<p>The <code>kat:schema</code> tree (short):</p>\n<pre>kat:VZCHU                kat:MZCHU                kat:OP\n  ├ kat:NP                 ├ kat:NPR\n  └ kat:CHKO               ├ kat:PR\n                           ├ kat:NPP\n                           └ kat:PP</pre>\n<pre>SELECT ?n WHERE &#123;\n  ?c skos:broader+ kat:VZCHU .      # all concepts below VZCHU\n  ?c skos:notation ?n .              # their codes\n&#125;                                    # result: NP, CHKO (2 rows)</pre>\n<p>With a star <code>skos:broader*</code> <code>kat:VZCHU</code> itself would be added (code <code>\"VZCHU\"</code>).</p>\n<p>Another vocabulary &mdash; IUCN: <code>?c skos:broader+ iucn:I</code> gives <code>Ia</code> and <code>Ib</code>; <code>skos:broader*</code> also <code>I</code>.</p>\n<p>Direction: <code>?c skos:broader X</code> reads \"?c has parent X\" &mdash; so <code>?c</code> is a <b>descendant</b> of X.</p>",
  "@lesson_24_theory": {
    "description": "Lesson 24 «SKOS: hierarchy via broader+»: theory",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_24_title": "SKOS: hierarchy via broader+",
  "@lesson_24_title": {
    "description": "Lesson 24 «SKOS: hierarchy via broader+»: title"
  },
