  "lesson_27_theory": "<p>How to refine a value (all <code>rml:…</code> from the <b>RML</b> vocabulary; <code>xsd:…</code> types from the <b>XSD</b> vocabulary):</p>\n<ul><li><code>rml:reference \"COLUMN\"</code> &mdash; the column value as is &rarr; a <b>literal</b></li>\n<li><code>rml:template \"…/&#123;COLUMN&#125;\"</code> &mdash; build an <b>address (IRI)</b>, e.g. a link to a SKOS concept</li>\n<li><code>rml:datatype xsd:…</code> &mdash; the literal's type (otherwise a plain string)</li>\n<li><code>rml:language \"cs\"</code> &mdash; language</li>\n<li><code>rml:constant</code> &mdash; the same value for all rows</li></ul>\n<p>Examples (on columns that are not in the task):</p>\n<pre># code as an integer\nrml:objectMap [ rml:reference \"KOD\" ; rml:datatype xsd:integer ]                  # \"110\"^^xsd:integer\n\n# change date from column ZMENA_G, already in YYYY-MM-DD form\nrml:objectMap [ rml:reference \"ZMENA_G\" ; rml:datatype xsd:date ]\n\n# link to a concept (IRI) built from column OP_TYP\nrml:objectMap [ rml:template \"https://kbss.fel.cvut.cz/bivak/typ-op/&#123;OP_TYP&#125;\" ]    # &lt;…/typ-op/ZAK&gt;\n\n# one value for every row\nrml:objectMap [ rml:constant bv:Example ]</pre>\n<p>Rule of thumb: <b>value is a number, date, yes/no, text</b> &rarr; <code>reference</code> + <code>datatype</code>; <b>value is a link to a thing or concept</b> &rarr; <code>template</code>.</p>\n<p>The strings <code>\"0\"</code> / <code>\"1\"</code> are valid values for <code>xsd:boolean</code>.</p>",
  "@lesson_27_theory": {
    "description": "Lesson 27 «RML: datatype and template»: theory",
    "context": "html"
  },
