  "lesson_2_theory": "<p>One thing is usually described by several triples. To avoid repeating the subject there are three shortcuts:</p>\n<ul><li><code>a</code> &mdash; \"is a\". Same as <code>rdf:type</code> (the \"type\" property from the <b>RDF</b> vocabulary, prefix <code>rdf:</code>).</li>\n<li><code>;</code> &mdash; \"more about the same one\" (next property of the same subject).</li>\n<li><code>,</code> &mdash; \"and one more value\" (same property, another value).</li></ul>\n<p>Without shortcuts:</p>\n<pre>:SpotA rdf:type :Spot .\n:SpotA rdfs:label \"Skalní převis\"@cs .\n:SpotA rdfs:label \"Rock overhang\"@en .\n:SpotA :liesWithin :NP_CeskeSvycarsko .</pre>\n<p>The same with shortcuts:</p>\n<pre>:SpotA a :Spot ;                              # type\n    rdfs:label \"Skalní převis\"@cs ,           # label 1\n               \"Rock overhang\"@en ;           # label 2 (comma = same property)\n    :liesWithin :NP_CeskeSvycarsko .          # full stop = end</pre>\n<p>Another example (a stay from bivak.ttl): <code>:Stay5 rdfs:label \"Stan na poli\"@cs ; :atSpot :SpotD .</code></p>",
  "@lesson_2_theory": {
    "description": "Lesson 2 «a, ; and ,»: theory",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_2_title": "a, ; and ,",
