  "lesson_4_theory": "<p>Sometimes a thing needs no name &mdash; it exists only as part of a description (\"some tarp on this trip\"). Write it right there in square brackets &mdash; a <mark>blank node</mark>:</p>\n<pre>:Stay1 :usesShelter [ a :Tarp ] ;                 # Stay1 has a tarp as shelter\n       :includesActivity [ a :Sleeping ] ,        # and two activities\n                         [ a :FoodPreparation ] .</pre>\n<p>This is shorthand for:</p>\n<pre>:Stay1 :usesShelter _:b1 .\n_:b1 a :Tarp .</pre>\n<p>Inside the brackets the same <code>a</code>, <code>;</code>, <code>,</code> work:</p>\n<pre>:Stay9 :usesShelter [ a :Tent ;\n                      rdfs:label \"My tent\"@en ] .</pre>",
