  "lesson_6_theory": "<p>The unknown can also be the <mark>relation</mark> itself. This asks \"what do we know about this node at all?\" &mdash; handy when you do not know the data:</p>\n<pre>SELECT ?p ?o\nWHERE &#123; :NP_Sumava ?p ?o . &#125;     # any property and any value</pre>\n<p>Result for <code>:NP_Sumava</code> (3 rows):</p>\n<pre>?p             ?o\nrdf:type       :NationalPark\nrdfs:label     \"Národní park Šumava\"@cs\nrdfs:label     \"Šumava National Park\"@en</pre>\n<p>The reverse question &mdash; \"what points to this node\" &mdash; moves the unknown: the node becomes the object.</p>\n<pre>SELECT ?s ?p\nWHERE &#123; ?s ?p :CHKO_Kokorinsko . &#125;     # who is linked to this CHKO (spot F, NPR Kokořínský důl)</pre>",
