  "lesson_77_hint_1": "Count countries with <code>GROUP BY</code> + <code>HAVING</code>; a value containing \" and \" means two countries: <code>SUM(IF(CONTAINS(STR(?c), \" and \"), 2, 1))</code>.",
  "@lesson_77_hint_1": {
    "description": "Lesson 77 «Task 2 – border summits»: hint 2",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_77_task": "Return the names of all border summits (lying in more than one country) with prominence over 300 m, most prominent first. Also output the prominence and the number of countries. Columns: <code>?name</code>, <code>?prominence</code>, <code>?countryCount</code>. <i>Prominence is stored as a string.</i> Catch: for Dufourspitze the country is a single value <code>\"Switzerland and Italy\"</code>. <div class=\"small\">Data: <code>four-thousanders.ttl</code> (82 summits). Prefixes: <code>uiaa-s: &lt;https://www.theuiaa.org/4000-alps/schema/&gt;</code>, <code>uiaa: &lt;https://www.theuiaa.org/4000-alps/summit/&gt;</code>. Ranges (<code>uiaa-s:inRange</code>) are bare IRIs with no names; output the IRI itself.</div>",
