  },
  "lesson_7_hint_0": "Two patterns on the variable ?spot: the type and <code>rdfs:label</code>.",
  "@lesson_7_hint_0": {
    "description": "Lesson 7 «Several patterns and ;»: hint 1",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_7_key": "Several triples in WHERE = AND; the shared variable ?x links them.",
  "@lesson_7_key": {
    "description": "Lesson 7 «Several patterns and ;»: the key point in one sentence",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_7_note_0": "Triples in WHERE combine as <b>AND</b>: a node is in the result only if it has both the type and the label.",
  "@lesson_7_note_0": {
    "description": "Lesson 7 «Several patterns and ;»: note box",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_7_note_1": "If a node has several labels it gives <b>several rows</b> &mdash; one per combination. The extras are removed by FILTER (next lesson) or DISTINCT.",
  "@lesson_7_note_1": {
    "description": "Lesson 7 «Several patterns and ;»: note box",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_7_note_2": "<code>SELECT DISTINCT</code> removes <b>completely identical</b> rows. It does not \"pick the best\" and does not change values: it only deletes repeats. Use it when joining triples (or paths, UNION) produced duplicates.",
  "@lesson_7_note_2": {
    "description": "Lesson 7 «Several patterns and ;»: note box",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_7_note_3": "<code>DISTINCT</code> goes after <code>SELECT</code>, not after <code>WHERE</code>: <code>SELECT DISTINCT ?spot WHERE &#123; … &#125;</code>. Do not confuse it with <code>COUNT(DISTINCT ?x)</code> &mdash; there it counts distinct values (GROUP BY lesson).",
  "@lesson_7_note_3": {
    "description": "Lesson 7 «Several patterns and ;»: note box",
    "context": "html"
  },
  "lesson_7_origin_0": "name",
  "@lesson_7_origin_0": {
